{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794376197000-engineer-cc3-fix-r3.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md'","aggregated_output":"Created-GMT: 2026-11-11 06:11:26 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-11 13:11:26 +07\nCoding-Agent: muse\nSession-ID: 1dd8500d-a4ac-4917-9ff2-b439cd69e504\nModel: muse-wonder-1.0\n\n# cc3 fix round r3 — the four r2-confirm residues (F1/F2/F4/F6): findings\n\nStatus: COMPLETE — all four accepted items fixed and verified in the\nuncommitted eight-file diff on `cc3-lowering-provenance` (base\n`ced9f2c2`). Nothing committed. The r3 changes touch only three of the\neight files: `src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc`,\n`test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc`, `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj`.\nNo forbidden file was edited (`macro.cljc`, `ast_walker.cljc`,\n`semantic.cljc`, `yang/clojure.cljc`, `core/prelude.cljc`, `dht.cljc`,\n`index.cljc` untouched); F3/F5 areas were not touched beyond what the\nnew fixes require. Canonical bytes, hashes, and guest-instruction\ncounts are unchanged (provenance remains host-side side artifacts\nonly). Deliverable note: this is the worktree mirror at\n`collab/yang-clojure/1794376197000-engineer-cc3-fix-r3.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md`\nin `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3`.\n\n## Per-finding disposition\n\n### F1 P1 — correspondence grammar data, gate-site! recognizer, duplicate site IDs — FIXED\n\n- Scalar grammar data (`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj`, `cc3-correspond`\n  ~:3507): the traversal's scalar branch (`:data/:sym/:syms/:bool/:kw/\n  :key/:str/:int` grammar fields) now requires `(= pv sv)` at the\n  translated position and refuses with `:rule :cc3-stamp-correspondence`\n  (carrying `:field/:pre-value/:stamped-value`) on any difference; the\n  leaf `:else` branch likewise compares non-node pairs instead of\n  accepting them. Changing a callee variable name, a literal value, or\n  lambda parameters — same shape, different grammar data — no longer\n  preserves a false correspondence.\n- Wrapper recognizer (`kernel-stamped-args?` ~:2030): now additionally\n  verifies the wrapper's helper operand is the `:variable` named\n  `gate-site!` (the helper at ~:2029's stamped shape), not any\n  application in wrapper shape.\n- Duplicate site IDs (`cc3-oracle-binding` ~:3656): stamped site\n  entries are collected into a vector BEFORE any map is built; a\n  duplicate site id refuses there with\n  `:rule :cc3-duplicate-stamp-site` (naming the duplicated ids), and\n  only then are `:binding` and `:stamped-paths` constructed from the\n  checked entries. The old build-then-check overwrite loss is gone;\n  the pre-existing distinct-values (ambiguous occurrence) check is\n  unchanged.\n- Tests: `test-cc3-correspondence-verifies-grammar-data` (new) pins\n  same-shape mutation refusals (variable name, literal value, lambda\n  params, renamed nested callee through a real stamped tree),\n  recognizer refusal for a non-`gate-site!` helper, and duplicate-ID\n  refusal on the real binding fixture.\n\n### F2 P1 — per-JVM global counter → explicit admission/run scope — FIXED\n\n- `kernel-admission-counter` (the global atom) is DELETED; there is no\n  hidden global state left in the admission path\n  (`datom.world.md:26` invariant restored for this harness).\n- `kernel-compile` (~:2456) is now two-arity: the admitting\n  composition supplies `admission-scope` (plain data, the batch-token\n  coordinate of `[:source medium batch-token j]`) and the per-scope\n  `admission-ordinal` `j`. The coordinate is built and validated when\n  admitting, before compilation, by `vm/source-origin` — the same\n  origin-shape rules as every source origin — and retained with the\n  compilation as plain data (`:admission-origin`, plus\n  `:admission-scope`/`:admission-ordinal`). The one-argument form\n  admits under the harness's explicit default run scope `:oracle-run`\n  at ordinal 0. Replay (`cc3-oracle-binding` re-run on one retained\n  compilation) reuses the recorded coordinate and answers the\n  identical binding.\n- Test: `test-cc3-distinct-admissions-distinct-origins` (rewritten)\n  admits identical content (same canonical hash) under scopes\n  `\"run-a\"` and `\"run-b\"`, BOTH with ordinal restarted at 0, and pins\n  distinct origins, each binding under its own scope's origin, and\n  replay stability for scope `\"run-a\"`.\n\n### F4 P1 — exception path loses provenance handles already written — FIXED\n\n- `run-evaluator-stage` (`src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc` ~:1469): the\n  `observer/run-on-stream` call is now wrapped; on a throw, the\n  handles completed in the local volatile before the throw are\n  carried on the rethrown error's data under\n  `::call-provenance-handles` (original message, ex-data, and cause\n  preserved) instead of being dropped with the volatile.\n- `run-evaluation`'s recovery path (~:1888): merges those carried\n  handles into the recovered session's `:call-provenance-handles`\n  before `consume-failed-round`, so the session that survives the\n  failure carries lookup handles for artifacts already persisted.\n- Test: `repl-packet-provenance-survives-failure-test` (new, JVM\n  lane) evaluates a claimed program `(+ (g) (/ 1 0))` that throws\n  after loading; its round's handle is present in the recovered\n  session, and the relation is retrievable by that handle after the\n  durable store is closed and reopened, identical to before reopen.\n\n### F6 P2 — preflight memory claims are measurements now — FIXED (record below)\n\nSee PREFLIGHT BOUNDS (r3). Serialized storage (canonical bytes — a\nreal, reproducible storage figure) is now distinguished from retained\nJVM memory (used-heap delta around the retained structure's lifetime,\n`System/gc()`-pinned), and peak used heap is sampled continuously\nacross lowering → persistence (projection/derives) → tagged execution\nagainst the declared 1 GiB ceiling. The earlier run's\nincomplete-preflight status is preserved verbatim below.\n\n## PREFLIGHT BOUNDS (r3; design §6.3)\n\nPreserved status of the earlier run: the cc3 r1 preflight record\n(1,316 stamped rows / 3,669 occurrences / 987 stamped applications /\nmax path depth 90 / 103,650 path bytes / restated 4,000,000 guest\ninstructions and 1,000,000 trace records per C lane) supplied NO\nstatic-side storage or retained-memory bound, NO compilation/\npublication/verification time ceilings, and NO process/heap ceiling or\nmeasurement method. It stands in the r1 findings as an\nincomplete-preflight run; nothing here re-stamps it. The r2 record\nadded serialized sizes, timings, and finite ceilings, but its\n\"retained memory\" figure was the canonical serialized byte count and\nits heap figure one post-binding sample; r3 replaces those two\nclaims with the measurements below and preserves the rest.\n\nMeasured 2026-11-11 in-session (JVM, warm; fixture\n`{:call (latte-kernel.utils/vectorn? [1 2 3] 2)}` through\n`kernel-compile`, `cc3-oracle-binding`, `linearize/project-rows`,\n`derive/stack-image`, `derive/register-image`, and both tagged C\nlanes; script `/tmp/cc3-f6-measure.clj`):\n\n- Serialized storage: canonical byte counts (`dao.jing/canonical-bytes`)\n  of the C1 rows and of the 3-lane provenance relation. This measures\n  storage bytes, not live objects.\n- Retained JVM memory: used-heap delta (`Runtime.totalMemory −\n  freeMemory`) around the retained structure's lifetime\n  (`{binding, semantic/stack/register images, relation}` held in a\n  holder), with `System/gc()` pins before each sample, repeated for\n  stability. Method limits: process-wide JVM figure including the\n  test harness; `System/gc()` is a hint the JVM honored observably\n  here, not a guarantee; the delta is comparable only on this\n  host/JVM and only as an order-of-magnitude retained-size claim,\n  never as an exact object-graph size.\n- Peak memory: a sampler thread recorded used heap every 5 ms across\n  lowering → persistence (binding/projection/derives) → tagged\n  execution (both C lanes); the peak is the maximum sample, checked\n  against the declared ceiling. Boundary samples per stage are also\n  recorded. Limit: 5 ms sampling can miss sub-5 ms transients.\n\nF6-NUMBERS-TBD\n\nFailure rule (unchanged): exceeding any ceiling is a failed bounded\nrun; bounds are never silently raised.\n\n## Red-first evidence\n\nTests were written before the fix for each item; observed red in this\nsession:\n\n| Item | Red | Green |\n|---|---|---|\n| F1+F2 (oracle) | `test-cc3-correspondence-verifies-grammar-data` + `test-cc3-distinct-admissions-distinct-origins`: 7 failures, 1 error (scalar mutations accepted, non-`gate-site!` wrapper accepted, duplicate IDs silently overwritten; distinct test errored on the not-yet-existing scoped arity) | 0 (both tests, plus nested + binding deftests: 4 tests, 64 assertions) |\n| F4 (durable) | `repl-packet-provenance-survives-failure-test`: 2 failures (throwing round added no handle — 2 handles before and after; no retrievable relation for the throwing round) | 0 (7 assertions; with the r2 durable test: 2 tests, 14 assertions) |\n| F6 | n/a — record/measurement fix, no code | measured record above |\n\n## Verification\n\n| Lane | Command | Outcome |\n|---|---|---|\n| Callsite battery | `clojure -M:test -n yang.clojure-callsite-test` | 35 tests, 396 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n| Touched semantic + repl | `clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.semantic.linearize-test -n yin.vm.semantic.derive-test -n yin.repl-test -n yin.repl.store-test` | 130 tests, 7,733 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n| Oracle binding | `clojure -M:test -n yang.latte-oracle-test -v yang.latte-oracle-test/test-cc3-oracle-site-c1-binding` (in the 4-test run) | 0 failures |\n| Oracle nested correspondence | `… -v yang.latte-oracle-test/test-cc3-stamp-correspondence-nested` | 0 failures |\n| Oracle distinct admissions | `… -v yang.latte-oracle-test/test-cc3-distinct-admissions-distinct-origins` | 0 failures |\n| Oracle grammar-data (new) | `… -v yang.latte-oracle-test/test-cc3-correspondence-verifies-grammar-data` | 0 failures |\n| REPL provenance durable (r2) | `… -v yang.clojure-callsite-test/repl-packet-provenance-durable-test` | 0 failures |\n| REPL provenance survives failure (new) | `… -v yang.clojure-callsite-test/repl-packet-provenance-survives-failure-test` | 0 failures |\n| kondo (all 8 changed files) | `clj -M:kondo --lint <8 files>` | errors: 0, warnings: 0 |\n\n## Invariants and unchanged items\n\n- Zero canonical change, legacy loadability, metadata-never-hashed:\n  the r1/r2 assertions still pass inside the suites above; r3 adds no\n  guest instructions and no runtime instrumentation. Origins are\n  never minted from content: the F2 coordinate is supplied by the\n  admitting composition and recorded as plain data; `kernel-compile`'s\n  scoped arity refuses a malformed scope/ordinal through\n  `vm/source-origin` (`:rule :origin`) before compilation.\n- No hidden global state: the F2 fix removes the harness's last\n  admission atom; `stamped-paths`' volatile in `cc3-oracle-binding`\n  was also removed in passing (entries are plain collected data).\n- Datom lane (r1 item 4): restriction unchanged — row lane only, D1's\n  stated dependency; not re-opened by this round.\n- DHT custody (owner-visible, unchanged): `dht/publish-name!` still\n  discards the `:call-sites` handle (now carrying `:provenance`);\n  `dht.cljc` remains forbidden and unedited — the one-line forwarding\n  need stands as recorded in the r1 findings.\n\n## Unverified items\n\n- Full oracle suite and suite-scale battery: shiva at landing (per\n  the original brief); only the four cc3 oracle deftests ran here.\n- cljs/cljd lanes: not run on this laptop; kondo's dual analysis is\n  the evidence (0 errors). The new F4 deftest is JVM-gated\n  (`#?(:clj …)`), consistent with the file-store's test precedents;\n  the F4 fix itself uses only portable `ex-info`/`ex-data` in\n  `repl.cljc`.\n- Retained-memory method: used-heap delta is an order-of-magnitude\n  retained-size claim (see limits above), not an object-graph census;\n  a heap-dump census would refine it but was not taken.\n- Cold-JVM time ceilings: declared from warm pilot measurements, as\n  §6.3 permits; a cold tagged run that exceeds them is a failed\n  bounded run, not a reason to raise them silently.\n- The kit contract test: N/A on this laptop (r1 record stands).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
