                           (map (fn [[o rr pth _ _]] [o rr pth])))\n  3653\t                                   r)\n  3654\t             :stamped-eligible (into #{}\n  3655\t                                     (map (fn [[rr pth]] [origin rr pth]))\n  3656\t                                     (vm/application-occurrences t))})\n  3657\t          correspondence (cc3-correspond ast (:ast compiled) [] [] {})\n  3658\t          ;; site entries are collected BEFORE any map is built: a\n  3659\t          ;; duplicate site id refuses here, never overwrites an\n  3660\t          ;; earlier occurrence in a map under construction (r3 F1)\n  3661\t          site-entries (into []\n  3662\t                             (comp (filter (fn [[_ node]]\n  3663\t                                             (= :application (:type node))))\n  3664\t                                   (keep (fn [[path node]]\n  3665\t                                           (let [direct (cc3-stamp-site-id\n  3666\t                                                          (second (:operands node)))\n  3667\t                                                 inner (kernel-routed-call? node)\n  3668\t                                                 routed (when inner\n  3669\t                                                          (cc3-stamp-site-id\n  3670\t                                                            (first (:operands inner))))]\n  3671\t                                             (when-let [k (or direct routed)]\n  3672\t                                               (let [pre-path (get correspondence\n  3673\t                                                                   path\n  3674\t                                                                   ::unmapped)]\n  3675\t                                                 (when (= ::unmapped pre-path)\n  3676\t                                                   (throw (ex-info\n  3677\t                                                            \"Stamped site has no pre-stamp correspondence\"\n  3678\t                                                            {:rule :cc3-stamp-correspondence\n  3679\t                                                             :site k\n  3680\t                                                             :stamped-path path})))\n  3681\t                                                 (let [key [origin (:root tree) pre-path]]\n  3682\t                                                   (when-not (contains? marked key)\n  3683\t                                                     (throw (ex-info\n  3684\t                                                              \"Stamped site maps to no validated C1 occurrence\"\n  3685\t                                                              {:rule :cc3-stamp-correspondence\n  3686\t                                                               :site k\n  3687\t                                                               :key key})))\n  3688\t                                                   [k path key])))))))\n  3689\t                             (cc3-walk (:ast compiled) [] []))\n  3690\t          _ (when (not= (count site-entries)\n  3691\t                        (count (into #{} (map first site-entries))))\n  3692\t              (throw (ex-info \"Duplicate stamped site id\"\n  3693\t                              {:rule :cc3-duplicate-stamp-site\n  3694\t                               :sites (vec (sort (into []\n  3695\t                                                       (comp (filter (fn [[_ n]]\n  3696\t                                                                       (< 1 n)))\n  3697\t                                                             (map first))\n  3698\t                                                       (frequencies\n  3699\t                                                         (map first\n  3700\t                                                              site-entries)))))})))\n  3701\t          stamped-paths (into {}\n  3702\t                              (map (fn [[k path _key]] [k path]))\n  3703\t                              site-entries)\n  3704\t          stamped-sites (into {}\n  3705\t                              (map (fn [[k _path key]] [k key]))\n  3706\t                              site-entries)]\n  3707\t      (when (not= (count stamped-sites)\n  3708\t                  (count (into #{} (vals stamped-sites))))\n  3709\t        (throw (ex-info \"Two stamped sites map to one pre-stamp occurrence\"\n  3710\t                        {:rule :cc3-ambiguous-stamp-correspondence\n  3711\t                         :binding stamped-sites})))\n  3712\t      {:origin origin :tree tree :rows rows :marked marked\n  3713\t       :eligible eligible :binding stamped-sites\n  3714\t       :correspondence correspondence\n  3715\t       :stamped-paths stamped-paths\n  3716\t       :stamped-tree stamped-tree :stamped-rows stamped-rows\n  3717\t       :stamped-marked stamped-marked\n  3718\t       :stamped-eligible stamped-eligible})))\n  3719\t\n  3720\t\n  3904\t(deftest test-cc3-correspondence-verifies-grammar-data\n  3905\t  ;; cc3 r3 item F1: correspondence must verify scalar grammar data at\n  3906\t  ;; translated positions, the wrapper recognizer must verify the\n  3907\t  ;; helper is gate-site!, and duplicate site ids must refuse before\n  3908\t  ;; any site map is constructed.\n  3909\t  (let [lit (fn [v] {:type :literal :value v})\n  3910\t        var* (fn [n] {:type :variable :name n})\n  3911\t        app (fn [op ops] {:type :application :operator op :operands ops})\n  3912\t        intra (fn [f args] (app (var* 'dsg__intra_call) [(var* f) args]))\n  3913\t        conj-args (fn [& xs] (app (var* 'conj) (into [(lit [])] xs)))\n  3914\t        inner (intra 'f (conj-args (lit 41)))\n  3915\t        outer (intra 'g (conj-args inner (lit 7)))\n  3916\t        {stamped :ast} (kernel-stamp-sites outer #{'f 'g})\n  3917\t        refusal (fn [pre stamped-tree]\n  3918\t                  (try (cc3-correspond pre stamped-tree [] [] {})\n  3919\t                       ::no-failure\n  3920\t                       (catch Exception e (:rule (ex-data e)))))]\n  3921\t    (testing \"same-shape scalar mutations refuse\"\n  3922\t      (is (= :cc3-stamp-correspondence\n  3923\t             (refusal (var* 'f) (var* 'h)))\n  3924\t          \"a changed callee variable name preserves shape but not grammar data\")\n  3925\t      (is (= :cc3-stamp-correspondence\n  3926\t             (refusal (lit 41) (lit 42)))\n  3927\t          \"a changed literal value preserves shape but not grammar data\")\n  3928\t      (is (= :cc3-stamp-correspondence\n  3929\t             (refusal {:type :lambda :params '[x] :body (lit 1)}\n  3930\t                      {:type :lambda :params '[y] :body (lit 1)}))\n  3931\t          \"changed lambda parameters preserve shape but not grammar data\")\n  3932\t      (let [entries (cc3-walk stamped [] [])\n  3933\t            callee-path (some (fn [[p node]]\n  3934\t                                (when (and (= :application (:type node))\n  3935\t                                           (= 'f (get-in node [:operands 0 :name])))\n  3936\t                                  p))\n  3937\t                              entries)\n  3938\t            mutated (cc3-assoc-at stamped callee-path\n  3939\t                                   (fn [node]\n  3940\t                                     (assoc-in node [:operands 0 :name] 'h)))]\n  3941\t        (is (some? callee-path))\n  3942\t        (is (= :cc3-stamp-correspondence (refusal outer mutated))\n  3943\t            \"a renamed nested callee refuses through the stamped tree\")))\n  3944\t    (testing \"the wrapper recognizer verifies the gate-site! helper\"\n  3945\t      (let [wrapper (some (fn [[_ node]]\n  3946\t                            (when (kernel-stamped-args? node) node))\n  3947\t                          (cc3-walk stamped [] []))\n  3948\t            mutated (assoc-in wrapper [:operands 0 :operands 0 :name]\n  3949\t                              'not-gate-site!)]\n  3950\t        (is (some? wrapper) \"precondition: a real stamping wrapper exists\")\n  3951\t        (is (nil? (kernel-stamped-args? mutated))\n  3952\t            \"a 3-arg application around another helper is no wrapper\")\n  3953\t        (is (= :cc3-stamp-correspondence (refusal outer\n  3954\t                                                  (cc3-assoc-at\n  3955\t                                                    stamped\n  3956\t                                                    (some (fn [[p node]]\n  3957\t                                                            (when (identical? node wrapper) p))\n  3958\t                                                          (cc3-walk stamped [] []))\n  3959\t                                                    (fn [_] mutated))))\n  3960\t            \"correspondence refuses when the wrapper helper is not gate-site!\")))\n  3961\t    (testing \"duplicate site ids refuse before map construction\"\n  3962\t      (let [fixture {:id :cc3-binding\n  3963\t                     :call '(latte-kernel.utils/vectorn? [1 2 3] 2)}\n  3964\t            compiled (kernel-compile fixture)\n  3965\t            wrappers (into []\n  3966\t                           (filter (fn [[_ node]]\n  3967\t                                     (kernel-stamped-args? node)))\n  3968\t                           (cc3-walk (:ast compiled) [] []))\n  3969\t            [p2 _] (second wrappers)\n  3970\t            k (cc3-stamp-site-id (second (first wrappers)))\n  3971\t            duplicated (cc3-assoc-at (:ast compiled) p2\n  3972\t                                      (fn [w]\n  3973\t                                        (assoc-in w [:operands 0 :operands 1\n  3974\t                                                     :operands 1 :value]\n  3975\t                                                  k)))]\n  3976\t        (is (= :compiled (:status compiled)))\n  3977\t        (is (<= 2 (count wrappers)) \"precondition: at least two stamped sites\")\n  3978\t        (is (some? k))\n  3979\t        (is (= :cc3-duplicate-stamp-site\n  3980\t               (try (cc3-oracle-binding (assoc compiled :ast duplicated))\n  3981\t                    ::no-failure\n  3982\t                    (catch Exception e (:rule (ex-data e)))))\n  3983\t            \"two wrappers carrying one site id refuse, never overwrite\")))))\n  3984\t\n  3985\t\n  3986\t(deftest test-cc3-distinct-admissions-distinct-origins\n  3987\t  ;; cc3 r3 item F2: the admission coordinate is an explicit,\n  3988\t  ;; composition-supplied scope plus a per-scope ordinal, retained\n  3989\t  ;; with the compilation as plain data — no per-JVM global counter.\n  3990\t  ;; Two scopes whose ordinals both restarted at 0, admitting\n  3991\t  ;; identical content, mint distinct origins; replaying one retained\n  3992\t  ;; admission (the binding test above) keeps its one origin.\n  3993\t  (let [fixture {:id :cc3-binding\n  3994\t                 :call '(latte-kernel.utils/vectorn? [1 2 3] 2)}\n  3995\t        a (kernel-compile fixture \"run-a\" 0)\n  3996\t        b (kernel-compile fixture \"run-b\" 0)]\n  3997\t    (is (= :compiled (:status a)))\n  3998\t    (is (= :compiled (:status b)))\n  3999\t    (is (= (:canonical-source-hash a) (:canonical-source-hash b))\n  4000\t        \"precondition: the content really is identical\")\n  4001\t    (is (= 0 (nth (:admission-origin a) 3) (nth (:admission-origin b) 3))\n  4002\t        \"precondition: both scopes restarted their ordinal at 0\")\n  4003\t    (is (= \"run-a\" (nth (:admission-origin a) 2)))\n  4004\t    (is (= \"run-b\" (nth (:admission-origin b) 2)))\n  4005\t    (is (not= (:admission-origin a) (:admission-origin b))\n  4006\t        \"distinct scopes with restarted ordinals mint distinct origins\")\n  4007\t    (let [ba (cc3-oracle-binding a)\n  4008\t          bb (cc3-oracle-binding b)]\n  4009\t      (is (= (:admission-origin a) (:origin ba)))\n  4010\t      (is (= (:admission-origin b) (:origin bb)))\n  4011\t      (is (= (:binding ba) (:binding (cc3-oracle-binding a)))\n  4012\t          \"replay reuses the recorded coordinate of scope run-a\")\n  4013\t      (is (= (set (keys (:binding ba))) (set (keys (:binding bb)))))\n  4014\t      (is (not= (set (vals (:binding ba))) (set (vals (:binding bb))))\n  4015\t          \"the same sites bind under each admission's own origin\"))))\n   113\tmeasurement method. It stands in the r1 findings as an\n   114\tincomplete-preflight run; nothing here re-stamps it. The r2 record\n   115\tadded serialized sizes, timings, and finite ceilings, but its\n   116\t\"retained memory\" figure was the canonical serialized byte count and\n   117\tits heap figure one post-binding sample; r3 replaces those two\n   118\tclaims with the measurements below and preserves the rest.\n   119\t\n   120\tMeasured 2026-11-11 in-session (JVM, warm; fixture\n   121\t`{:call (latte-kernel.utils/vectorn? [1 2 3] 2)}` through\n   122\t`kernel-compile`, `cc3-oracle-binding`, `linearize/project-rows`,\n   123\t`derive/stack-image`, `derive/register-image`, and both tagged C\n   124\tlanes; script `/tmp/cc3-f6-measure.clj`):\n   125\t\n   126\t- Serialized storage: canonical byte counts (`dao.jing/canonical-bytes`)\n   127\t  of the C1 rows and of the 3-lane provenance relation. This measures\n   128\t  storage bytes, not live objects.\n   129\t- Retained JVM memory: used-heap delta (`Runtime.totalMemory −\n   130\t  freeMemory`) around the retained structure's lifetime\n   131\t  (`{binding, semantic/stack/register images, relation}` held in a\n   132\t  holder), with `System/gc()` pins before each sample, repeated for\n   133\t  stability. Method limits: process-wide JVM figure including the\n   134\t  test harness; `System/gc()` is a hint the JVM honored observably\n   135\t  here, not a guarantee; the delta is comparable only on this\n   136\t  host/JVM and only as an order-of-magnitude retained-size claim,\n   137\t  never as an exact object-graph size.\n   138\t- Peak memory: a sampler thread recorded used heap every 5 ms across\n   139\t  lowering → persistence (binding/projection/derives) → tagged\n   140\t  execution (both C lanes); the peak is the maximum sample, checked\n   141\t  against the declared ceiling. Boundary samples per stage are also\n   142\t  recorded. Limit: 5 ms sampling can miss sub-5 ms transients.\n   143\t\n   144\tF6-NUMBERS-TBD\n   145\t\n   146\tFailure rule (unchanged): exceeding any ceiling is a failed bounded\n   147\trun; bounds are never silently raised.\n   148\t\n   149\t## Red-first evidence\n   150\t\n   151\tTests were written before the fix for each item; observed red in this\n   152\tsession:\n   153\t\n   154\t| Item | Red | Green |\n   155\t|---|---|---|\n   156\t| F1+F2 (oracle) | `test-cc3-correspondence-verifies-grammar-data` + `test-cc3-distinct-admissions-distinct-origins`: 7 failures, 1 error (scalar mutations accepted, non-`gate-site!` wrapper accepted, duplicate IDs silently overwritten; distinct test errored on the not-yet-existing scoped arity) | 0 (both tests, plus nested + binding deftests: 4 tests, 64 assertions) |\n   157\t| F4 (durable) | `repl-packet-provenance-survives-failure-test`: 2 failures (throwing round added no handle — 2 handles before and after; no retrievable relation for the throwing round) | 0 (7 assertions; with the r2 durable test: 2 tests, 14 assertions) |\n   158\t| F6 | n/a — record/measurement fix, no code | measured record above |\n   159\t\n   160\t## Verification\n   161\t\n   162\t| Lane | Command | Outcome |\n   163\t|---|---|---|\n   164\t| Callsite battery | `clojure -M:test -n yang.clojure-callsite-test` | 35 tests, 396 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n   165\t| Touched semantic + repl | `clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.semantic.linearize-test -n yin.vm.semantic.derive-test -n yin.repl-test -n yin.repl.store-test` | 130 tests, 7,733 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n   166\t| Oracle binding | `clojure -M:test -n yang.latte-oracle-test -v yang.latte-oracle-test/test-cc3-oracle-site-c1-binding` (in the 4-test run) | 0 failures |\n   167\t| Oracle nested correspondence | `… -v yang.latte-oracle-test/test-cc3-stamp-correspondence-nested` | 0 failures |\n   168\t| Oracle distinct admissions | `… -v yang.latte-oracle-test/test-cc3-distinct-admissions-distinct-origins` | 0 failures |\n   169\t| Oracle grammar-data (new) | `… -v yang.latte-oracle-test/test-cc3-correspondence-verifies-grammar-data` | 0 failures |\n   170\t| REPL provenance durable (r2) | `… -v yang.clojure-callsite-test/repl-packet-provenance-durable-test` | 0 failures |\n   171\t| REPL provenance survives failure (new) | `… -v yang.clojure-callsite-test/repl-packet-provenance-survives-failure-test` | 0 failures |\n   172\t| kondo (all 8 changed files) | `clj -M:kondo --lint <8 files>` | errors: 0, warnings: 0 |\n   173\t\n   174\t## Invariants and unchanged items\n   175\t\n   176\t- Zero canonical change, legacy loadability, metadata-never-hashed:\n   177\t  the r1/r2 assertions still pass inside the suites above; r3 adds no\n   178\t  guest instructions and no runtime instrumentation. Origins are\n   179\t  never minted from content: the F2 coordinate is supplied by the\n   180\t  admitting composition and recorded as plain data; `kernel-compile`'s\n   181\t  scoped arity refuses a malformed scope/ordinal through\n   182\t  `vm/source-origin` (`:rule :origin`) before compilation.\n   183\t- No hidden global state: the F2 fix removes the harness's last\n   184\t  admission atom; `stamped-paths`' volatile in `cc3-oracle-binding`\n   185\t  was also removed in passing (entries are plain collected data).\n   186\t- Datom lane (r1 item 4): restriction unchanged — row lane only, D1's\n   187\t  stated dependency; not re-opened by this round.\n   188\t- DHT custody (owner-visible, unchanged): `dht/publish-name!` still\n   189\t  discards the `:call-sites` handle (now carrying `:provenance`);\n   190\t  `dht.cljc` remains forbidden and unedited — the one-line forwarding\n(require 'yang.latte-oracle-test 'dao.jing 'yin.vm.semantic.linearize 'yin.vm.semantic.derive)\n(def kc @#'yang.latte-oracle-test/kernel-compile)\n(def binding @#'yang.latte-oracle-test/cc3-oracle-binding)\n(def kernel-c @#'yang.latte-oracle-test/kernel-c)\n(import '(java.lang Runtime System))\n(def rt (Runtime/getRuntime))\n(defn used [] (- (.totalMemory rt) (.freeMemory rt)))\n(defn gc-used [] (System/gc) (Thread/sleep 50) (System/gc) (used))\n(def fixture {:id :cc3-binding :call '(latte-kernel.utils/vectorn? [1 2 3] 2)})\n;; peak sampler across lowering -> persistence(projection/derives) -> tagged execution\n(def peak (atom 0))\n(def stop (atom false))\n(def sampler (Thread. (fn [] (while (not @stop) (swap! peak max (used)) (Thread/sleep 5)))))\n(def t0 (System/currentTimeMillis))\n(def base (gc-used))\n(.start sampler)\n(def stage-peaks (atom []))\n(defn mark [label] (swap! stage-peaks conj [label (used)]))\n(def compiled (kc fixture)) (mark :after-compile)\n(def b (binding compiled)) (mark :after-binding)\n(def sem (yin.vm.semantic.linearize/project-rows (:tree b) nil (:rows b))) (mark :after-project-rows)\n(def stack (yin.vm.semantic.derive/stack-image (:vector sem) {:segment-address :seg/stack :call-provenance (:call-provenance sem)})) (mark :after-stack)\n(def reg (yin.vm.semantic.derive/register-image (:vector sem) {:segment-address :seg/register :call-provenance (:call-provenance sem)})) (mark :after-register)\n(def relation {:semantic (:call-provenance sem) :stack (:call-provenance stack) :register (:call-provenance reg)})\n(def c-walker (kernel-c compiled :c-walker)) (mark :after-c-walker)\n(def c-sem (kernel-c compiled :c-semantic)) (mark :after-c-semantic)\n(reset! stop true) (.join sampler)\n(def elapsed (- (System/currentTimeMillis) t0))\n;; serialized storage (canonical bytes) vs retained JVM objects (used-heap delta, gc-pinned)\n(def rows-bytes (count (dao.jing/canonical-bytes (:rows b))))\n(def rel-bytes (count (dao.jing/canonical-bytes relation)))\n(def retained-box (atom nil))\n(def before-retain (gc-used))\n(reset! retained-box {:binding b :sem sem :stack stack :reg reg :relation relation})\n(def after-retain (gc-used))\n;; repeat delta measurement for stability\n(def deltas (mapv (fn [_] (let [x (atom nil) b0 (gc-used)] (reset! x {:b b :s sem :st stack :r reg}) (let [a (gc-used)] (reset! x nil) (- a b0)))) (range 3)))\n(println :compiled-status (:status compiled))\n(println :c-status (:status c-walker) (:status c-sem))\n(println :rows-canonical-bytes rows-bytes)\n(println :relation-canonical-bytes rel-bytes)\n(println :heap-baseline-gc-used base)\n(println :stage-used stage-peaks)\n(println :peak-used-during-pipeline @peak)\n(println :peak-over-baseline (- @peak base))\n(println :retained-delta-first (- after-retain before-retain))\n(println :retained-deltas-repeat deltas)\n(println :elapsed-ms elapsed)\n(println :ceiling-bytes 1073741824 :peak-under-ceiling (< @peak 1073741824))\n(System/exit 0)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
